<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.5 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.5 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.5 percent in the week to April 16 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 3.1 percent.(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			    Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  20.99	  21.13	     19.89</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	2.12	   2.03		1.82</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
